  "name": "n8n Circuit Breaker - Auto-Disable Failing External APIs",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d1b39132-9d36-422f-9d7b-4ba6ab7c7514",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2064,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1200,
        "height": 1360,
        "content": "## n8n Circuit Breaker - Auto-Disable Failing External APIs\n\nA resilience wrapper that sits between your workflows and any flaky third-party API. Instead of calling the external API directly, callers hit this webhook with a service name. The breaker tracks failures per service in Redis and, once a threshold is crossed, **opens the circuit**: further calls are rejected instantly (503) without touching the failing API. After a cool-down it lets exactly one **half-open probe** through; success closes the circuit, failure re-opens it.\n\n### States\n- **CLOSED** - normal. Calls pass through, failures are counted.\n- **OPEN** - tripped. Calls are rejected fast with 503 + Retry-After.\n- **HALF_OPEN** - cool-down elapsed. One probe request is allowed; everyone else still gets 503.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Import this workflow into n8n\n2. Add the Redis credential on every Redis node\n3. Edit Set - Breaker Config: serviceRegistry (service -> baseUrl, optional per-service failureThreshold / openDurationSeconds), default failureThreshold, failureWindowSeconds, openDurationSeconds, requestTimeoutMs, alertWebhookUrl (Slack-compatible, optional)\n4. Point callers at POST /webhook/circuit-breaker with body { service, path, method, payload }\n5. Activate the workflow\n\n### Redis keys\n- `cb:{service}:state` - JSON { state, openedAt, reason, failureCount }\n- `cb:{service}:failures` - failure counter (TTL = failureWindowSeconds, refreshed on each failure)\n- `cb:{service}:probe:{openedAt}` - half-open probe claim (one per open cycle)\n\n### How to customize\n- Add 429 (or any status) to the failure rule in JS - Classify Outcome\n- Allow more than one half-open probe by raising the limit in JS - Evaluate Probe\n- Add a status/manual-reset webhook that reads, sets or deletes the state key\n- Put this gateway behind your RBAC API Gateway workflow for authenticated access\n- Redis errors fail OPEN on purpose (calls are allowed), so a Redis outage never takes your integrations down"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5936c941-37b5-403d-9906-4c68fd7e9f28",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Entry & Registry",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -624,
        496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 860,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## 1. Trigger, Config & Service Registry\n\nWebhook - Breaker Entry receives { service, path, method, payload }.\n\nSet - Breaker Config centralizes thresholds, timeouts and the serviceRegistry (the only URLs this workflow will ever call, which prevents it being used as an open proxy).\n\nJS - Resolve Service validates the service name and path, builds the target URL, applies per-service overrides and derives the Redis keys.\n\nIF - Service Registered sends unknown services / bad paths to a 404."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "469cb18a-d416-47eb-afdf-31d20f3ba7e7",
      "name": "Sticky Note - State Check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        288,
        496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## 2. Circuit State Check\n\nRedis - Get Breaker State reads the stored state for the service.\n\nJS - Evaluate Breaker State decides: CLOSED -> allow, OPEN and still cooling down -> reject, OPEN and cool-down elapsed -> HALF_OPEN probe.\n\nIF - Circuit Open short-circuits rejected calls to a 503 with Retry-After. IF - Is Half-Open Probe routes the trial request to the probe gate."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0c41d46d-3a89-42d8-bca9-17e0127f726a",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Half-Open Probe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1216,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 588,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## 3. Half-Open Probe Gate\n\nRedis - Claim Probe Slot does an INCR on a key unique to this open cycle. Only the first caller (count = 1) is granted the probe; everyone else gets a 503 so a recovering API is not stampeded."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f75233c8-479b-4970-b761-82a3f9f0f413",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Call & Classify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1840,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 636,
        "height": 488,
        "content": "## 4. Call External API & Classify\n\nHTTP Request - Call External API uses a timeout and never throws on HTTP errors, so every outcome reaches the classifier.\n\nJS - Classify Outcome marks the call as failed on network error / timeout, HTTP 5xx or 408. Other 4xx responses are client errors and do NOT count against the service."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5bb90445-f62b-4767-854f-a1f0bbdb2feb",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Success Path",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2512,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1116,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## 5. Success Path\n\nIf the call was a half-open probe and succeeded, Redis deletes the state and failure counter, closing the circuit. Normal CLOSED successes need no Redis write, which keeps the happy path cheap."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "13732149-8bf1-4dd3-8e6b-9bc4ece97495",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Failure Path",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2528,
        864
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1800,
        "height": 636,
        "content": "## 6. Failure Path & Trip Logic\n\nRedis - Increment Failure Counter counts failures within the window. JS - Evaluate Trip opens the circuit when the count reaches the threshold, or immediately if a half-open probe failed.\n\nRedis - Open Circuit stores the OPEN state with a timestamp. An optional alert is posted to alertWebhookUrl, then the caller gets a 502 describing the failure and the circuit status."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
